Congratulations indeed.

I seriously doubt that most of the people on
this list really appreciate the political mountains
that Stephen had to climb to make SELinux
what it is today. When I first meet with the
Flask team at NSA in late 1999 the whole
notion of the NSA making something freely
available was beyond credibility, even they
thought they required an outside conduit.
Today SELinux is the only real path for
advanced security development, and the
credit ought to go to Stephen for the hard
work he's put into making it so.


